<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enewetak</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Eniwetok</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enewetak is a large coral atoll in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marshall-islands">Marshall Islands</a>. American forces captured it from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in February 1944, and from 1948 to 1958 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> carried out 43 nuclear tests there, including Ivy Mike in 1952, the first full-scale hydrogen bomb. Its people were moved away and returned only after a partial clean-up in 1980; contaminated soil was sealed under the concrete Runit Dome.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/enewetak.jpg" alt="Enewetak" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Enewetak_Atoll_-_2014-02-10_-_Landsat_8_-_15m.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
